## D. Deprecated functionality & drop analysis

| Item | Producer(s) | Consumer(s) | Safe to drop cleanly? |
|---|---|---|---|
| `RequiredTargetUserspacePackages` (model, `@deprecated` 2021-10-10, replaced by `TargetUserSpacePreupgradeTasks`) | `cloud/checkrhui` **declares but never emits it** (stale decl) | this actor only | **Yes** — no live producer, replacement already consumed here. Edit both actors + this test. |
| `LEAPP_DEVEL_SKIP_RHSM` (env var) | — | this actor only (single file) | **Yes** — already only logs a warning; successor is `LEAPP_NO_RHSM`/`--no-rhsm`. |
| `TMPTargetRepositoriesFacts` (model, `@deprecated` 2020-09-01) | **this actor only** | **`adjustlocalrepos` + `missinggpgkeysinhibitor`** | **No — not internal.** See below. |

**The hole in "only internal changes":** dropping `TMPTargetRepositoriesFacts` is
an outside-world change. Two other actors consume it, and **no existing
non-deprecated model carries the same data** (target repofiles with full
baseurl/mirrorlist/gpgkey detail). `RepositoriesFacts` is the same *shape* but
semantically describes the *source* system — which is exactly why the temporary
model was created. So "replacing by a conceptual solution" here is a real design
task spanning three actors, not a delete. `RequiredTargetUserspacePackages` and
`LEAPP_DEVEL_SKIP_RHSM` are genuinely low-risk drops.

