## G. Refactor plan

Do this as **separate commits** so review can verify each: (1) pure module split
with zero logic change, (2) repofile-parse dedup, (3) model replacement +
migration, (4) deprecated drops.

### G1. Decompose `userspacegen.py` (behavior-preserving move)

Split the ~5 responsibilities into modules under the actor's `libraries/`
(imported as `leapp.libraries.actor.<name>`). `userspacegen.py` shrinks to
`perform()` + message production.

- `inputdata.py` — `InputData` (rename from `_InputData`) + `_consume_data`.
- `targetrhui.py` — `setup_target_rhui_access_if_needed`, `_apply_rhui_access_*`,
  `_get_rhui_available_repoids`, `_remove_injected_repofiles_from_our_rhui_packages`,
  `get_copy_location_from_copy_in_task`.
- `targetrepos.py` — `gather_target_repositories`, `_gather_target_repositories`,
  `_get_distro_available_repoids`, `_get_all_available_repoids`,
  `_inhibit_if_no_base_repos`, `_inhibit_on_duplicate_repos`,
  `_install_custom_repofiles`, `adjust_dnf_stream_variable`
  (+ `_get_product_certificate_path`). Keep `@suppress_deprecation(RHELTargetRepository)`
  (separate, out-of-scope deprecation).
- `bootstrap.py` — `prepare_target_userspace`, `_create_target_userspace`,
  `_create_target_userspace_directories`, `_import_gpg_keys`,
  `_handle_transaction_err_msg_size`, `_restore/_backup_to_persistent_package_cache`,
  `_copy_files`, `_get_target_userspace`.
- `repoaccess.py` (or `rpmfiles.py`) — `_prep_repository_access`,
  `_copy_certificates`, `_copy_decouple`, `_copy_symlinks`, `_choose_copy_or_link`,
  `_mkdir_with_copied_mode`, `_get_files_owned_by_rpms`, `_query_rpm_for_pkg_files`,
  `BrokenSymlinkError`.

Circular-import care: the two `rpm -qf/-ql` helpers are used by both RHUI and
repo-access code — give them one home (`repoaccess.py`) and import into
`targetrhui.py`; `repoaccess`/`rpmfiles` must not import `targetrhui`.

### G2. Repofile-parse dedup — narrower than #486 implies

**Honest scoping [High]:** repofiles are parsed at `_get_all_available_repoids`
(l.814, scratch overlay, pre-userspace) and again in `perform` (l.1425, *after*
`/etc/yum.repos.d` is rewritten). These parse the **same container in different
states** and **cannot be collapsed** without changing behavior. Real, safe dedup:
- Extract `parsed_repofiles_or_stop(context)` wrapping `repofileutils.get_parsed_repofiles`
  with the identical ~8-line StopActorExecutionError handler duplicated at
  l.815-821, 1316-1323, 1426-1434. Reuse at all three sites.
- Have `_get_all_available_repoids` **return the parsed repofiles list** (not just
  the repoid set) so the duplicate-repo inhibitor + repoid extraction share one
  parse. (This is the one change with a behavioral footprint — add a test that the
  duplicate-repo inhibitor still fires under `skip_rhsm`.)
- Out of scope: folding in `rhsm._inhibit_on_duplicate_repos` (l.782 TODO) — lives
  in shared `rhsm` lib, touches other actors.

### G3. Replace `TMPTargetRepositoriesFacts`

Consumers read the full `RepositoryFile`/`RepositoryData` shape:
`adjustlocalrepos` uses `.file`, `.repoid`, `.baseurl`, `.mirrorlist`;
`missinggpgkeysinhibitor` uses `.repoid`, `.additional_fields` (gpgkey/gpgcheck).
Same shape as `RepositoriesFacts` but for the **target** — can't reuse
`RepositoriesFacts` (already produced for the source; consumers run in target phase).

New model in `models/repositoriesfacts.py`, reusing existing `RepositoryFile`:
```python
class TargetRepositoriesFacts(Model):
    topic = SystemFactsTopic
    repositories = fields.List(fields.Model(RepositoryFile))
```
Only the type name changes — no consumer field-access change needed.

Migration (**one PR** — leapp validates consumed types exist):
- `targetuserspacecreator`: produce `TargetRepositoriesFacts`; drop the
  `@suppress_deprecation(TMPTargetRepositoriesFacts)` + deprecated import;
  update `actor.py` produces/imports.
- `adjustlocalrepos` + `missinggpgkeysinhibitor` (actor.py + `missinggpgkey.py`):
  swap import/consume; remove `@suppress_deprecation`; update docstrings/tests.
- Delete `TMPTargetRepositoriesFacts` from `models/repositoriesfacts.py` (deprecated
  2020, far past window; produced/consumed only in-repo, all updated atomically).
  Record removal + replacement in `docs/.../deprecations-list.md` "Next release".
- **Caveat [Medium]:** out-of-tree third-party consumers weren't exhaustively
  disproven. Model was marked temporary/internal, so risk is low; if the team wants
  belt-and-suspenders, keep it one release as
  `class TMPTargetRepositoriesFacts(TargetRepositoriesFacts)` and stop producing it.
  Recommendation: remove outright.

### G4. Drop remaining deprecated functionality

- `RequiredTargetUserspacePackages`: no live producer (`cloud/checkrhui`'s
  `produces` entry is stale — verified). Remove import/consume/decorator in this
  actor (`inputdata.py` + `actor.py`), the stale `produces` in
  `cloud/checkrhui/actor.py`, and test fixtures. Optionally delete the model
  (`models/targetuserspace.py:114-117`); note in deprecations-list.
- `LEAPP_DEVEL_SKIP_RHSM`: delete `_check_deprecated_rhsm_skip` (l.74-85) + its
  call in `perform` + stale comment (l.1401). Successor is `LEAPP_NO_RHSM`/`--no-rhsm`.

